second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"Inquiry about the residence would be: \\\"Where does Zdenko Schleissner reside?\\\"\", \"slot_hint\": \"other\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 78, \"text\": \"Title: The Unbroken Spirit of Zdenko Schleissner: A Holocaust Survivor's Story\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 80, \"end\": 235, \"text\": \"In the heart of the Czech Republic, where the Elbe River flows gently through the city, lies Hradec Králové, a place of rich history and cultural heritage.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 236, \"end\": 344, \"text\": \"It was here, in this very city, that Zdenko Schleissner, a young man born on February 28, 1918, called home.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 345, \"end\": 456, \"text\": \"Little did he know, his life was about to take a drastic turn, one that would test his resilience and humanity.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 457, \"end\": 574, \"text\": \"As the Nazi occupation of Czechoslovakia began in 1939, Zdenko's life, like that of many others, was forever changed.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 575, \"end\": 690, \"text\": \"The once peaceful streets of Hradec Králové were now filled with the sound of marching boots and the smell of fear.\"}, \"D1S7\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 691, \"end\": 834, \"text\": \"Zdenko, a Jew, was forced to confront the harsh reality of the Holocaust, a genocide that would claim the lives of six million innocent people.\"}, \"D1S8\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 835, \"end\": 939, \"text\": \"Despite the danger, Zdenko remained in Hradec Králové, determined to survive and resist the Nazi regime.\"}, \"D1S9\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 940, \"end\": 1027, \"text\": \"He continued to work as a clerk, using his skills to aid the local resistance movement.\"}, \"D1S10\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1028, \"end\": 1101, \"text\": \"His bravery and cunning allowed him to evade capture, at least initially.\"}, \"D1S11\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1102, \"end\": 1155, \"text\": \"However, on November 24, 1941, Zdenko's luck ran out.\"}, \"D1S12\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1156, \"end\": 1296, \"text\": \"He was arrested by the Gestapo and deported to the Theresienstadt concentration camp, a mere 100 kilometers from his beloved Hradec Králové.\"}, \"D1S13\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1297, \"end\": 1419, \"text\": \"The camp, disguised as a model ghetto, was in reality a transit point for Jews destined for the gas chambers of Auschwitz.\"}, \"D1S14\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1420, \"end\": 1487, \"text\": \"Zdenko's time in Theresienstadt was marked by hardship and despair.\"}, \"D1S15\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1488, \"end\": 1580, \"text\": \"He was forced to live in overcrowded and unsanitary conditions, with minimal food and water.\"}, \"D1S16\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1581, \"end\": 1666, \"text\": \"Yet, even in the face of such horror, he found ways to maintain his dignity and hope.\"}, \"D1S17\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1667, \"end\": 1862, \"text\": \"He formed close bonds with fellow prisoners, including the renowned Czech artist, Friedl Dicker-Brandeis, who would later become a symbol of the Holocaust's devastating impact on art and culture.\"}, \"D1S18\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1863, \"end\": 1963, \"text\": \"In 1944, Zdenko was transferred to Auschwitz, where he was subjected to the brutal regime of the SS.\"}, \"D1S19\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1964, \"end\": 2107, \"text\": \"He was forced to work in the camp's notorious Buna factory, where prisoners were worked to death under the guise of producing synthetic rubber.\"}, \"D1S20\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 2108, \"end\": 2222, \"text\": \"Despite the unimaginable conditions, Zdenko continued to resist, using his skills to sabotage the Nazi war effort.\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 148, \"text\": \"As the snowflakes gently fell onto the frozen lake, casting a serene silence over the small town of Polvijärvi, a lone figure emerged from the mist.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 149, \"end\": 313, \"text\": \"Zdenko Schleissner, a man with a worn face and piercing brown eyes, trudged through the snow-covered streets, his boots leaving behind a trail of faint impressions.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 314, \"end\": 478, \"text\": \"It was a chilly winter morning in 1943, and the war was raging on, but in this remote corner of North Karelia, Finland, life went on, albeit with a sense of unease.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 479, \"end\": 608, \"text\": \"Zdenko, a Czech Jew, had arrived in Polvijärvi a few months prior, seeking refuge from the horrors that had ravaged his homeland.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 609, \"end\": 702, \"text\": \"He had lost his family, his friends, and his sense of identity in the chaos of the Holocaust.\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 703, \"end\": 821, \"text\": \"The small town, nestled among the pine forests and lakes, had become his sanctuary, a place where he could start anew.\"}, \"D2S7\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 822, \"end\": 976, \"text\": \"As he walked, the sound of children's laughter carried on the wind, and Zdenko's gaze followed the noise to a small wooden cabin on the outskirts of town.\"}, \"D2S8\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 977, \"end\": 1087, \"text\": \"Smoke billowed from the chimney, and the aroma of freshly baked bread wafted out, enticing him to come closer.\"}, \"D2S9\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1088, \"end\": 1184, \"text\": \"He knocked on the door, and a kind-faced woman, Helmi, answered, her eyes sparkling with warmth.\"}, \"D2S10\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1185, \"end\": 1255, \"text\": \"\\\"Zdenko, dear, come in from the cold,\\\" she said, beckoning him inside.\"}, \"D2S11\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1256, \"end\": 1324, \"text\": \"\\\"I've made some karjalanpiirakka, just like my mother used to make.\\\"\"}, \"D2S12\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1325, \"end\": 1464, \"text\": \"Zdenko's eyes lit up at the mention of the traditional Karelian pasties, and he stepped inside, feeling a sense of belonging wash over him.\"}, \"D2S13\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1465, \"end\": 1626, \"text\": \"As he sat at the table, surrounded by Helmi's family, he began to open up, sharing stories of his past, of his family's struggles, and of his own narrow escapes.\"}, \"D2S14\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1627, \"end\": 1718, \"text\": \"The family listened with rapt attention, their faces etched with empathy and understanding.\"}, \"D2S15\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1719, \"end\": 1820, \"text\": \"They knew what it meant to be displaced, to be forced to flee from the only home they had ever known.\"}, \"D2S16\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1821, \"end\": 2010, \"text\": \"The war had brought its own set of challenges to Polvijärvi, but in this small community, they had learned to come together, to support one another, and to find solace in the simple things.\"}, \"D2S17\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 2011, \"end\": 2134, \"text\": \"As the afternoon wore on, Zdenko felt a sense of peace settle over him, a sense of belonging that he had not felt in years.\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"card_id\": \"d1:c0\", \"entity\": \"Zdenko Schleissner\", \"scope\": \"residence\", \"claim\": \"Zdenko Schleissner resides in Hradec Králové.\", \"answer\": \"Hradec Králové\", \"quote\": \"It was here, in this very city, that Zdenko Schleissner, a young man born on February 28, 1918, called home.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"card_id\": \"d2:c0\", \"entity\": \"Zdenko Schleissner\", \"scope\": \"residence\", \"claim\": \"Zdenko Schleissner resides in Polvijärvi.\", \"answer\": \"Polvijärvi\", \"quote\": \"Zdenko, a Czech Jew, had arrived in Polvijärvi a few months prior, seeking refuge from the horrors that had ravaged his homeland. He had lost his family, his friends, and his sense of identity in the chaos of the Holocaust. The small town, nestled among the pine forests and lakes, had become his sanctuary, a place where he could start anew.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}], \"R5_answers\": [\"Hradec Králové\", \"Polvijärvi\"], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"Hradec Králové\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C1\", \"answer\": \"Polvijärvi\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}]}"
